WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Hey y'all, Dr. Jill with Central Dentist here.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.000
I'm super excited. All four of my kids are back in school.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:11.000
I'm back in the office. I hope your kids are in school and you're getting into your new routine.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:17.000
I'm looking through some of these charts and wondering if there's an opportunity for a little more education.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:21.000
We've talked about those silver fillings you have in your mouth. That's why I'm reaching out to you.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:27.000
Those silver fillings contain mercury. An intact filling doesn't automatically mean it's causing a health problem,

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:35.000
but that mercury vapor is released in small amounts over time, particularly with chewing, grinding, hot coffee, or cold water.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:44.000
So from a biological dentistry perspective, our goal is to reduce unnecessary exposure to materials that may add to your overall toxic burden.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:53.000
Because those fillings also crack and age and can contribute to fractures around the tooth, it's important to replace them when it's time,

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:54.500
rather than waiting for a problem.

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:58.000
So if you choose removal, as a reminder, we use the SMART protocol.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:06.000
We have special isolation, high-volume suction, air filtration, and other protective measures designed to minimize mercury exposure during the procedure.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:13.000
So we can prioritize the fillings that are the largest, the oldest, or showing signs of breakdown, and create a plan that feels manageable to you.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:15.000
Reach out. We'd love to help you.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:23.000
We're here and ready to finish the year decreasing our toxic burden, so 2027 can be our healthiest year yet.
